/*
 * ------------------------------------------------------------
 * IMPORTANT: The contents of this file are auto-generated.
 *
 * This file may be updated by the Shopify admin theme editor
 * or related systems. Please exercise caution as any changes
 * made to this file may be overwritten.
 * ------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * Why this file exists as a copy of templates/article.json: every Brew Guides
 * article actually linked to a live product (confirmed live via the Admin API
 * templateSuffix field -- Kagumo AB, Kaliluni AA, Regional Aurea, Bridazul Lot 1,
 * Janson Estate, Kiambu Regional C, Raspberry Candy Filter, Thageini Karibu, and
 * more) carries template_suffix "article", which Shopify resolves to
 * templates/article.article.json -- not the default templates/article.json.
 * Without this file, those articles silently fell back to Horizon's bare
 * main-blog-post layout (title/date/image/content only), which is why PR #282's
 * fix to templates/article.json never appeared on any article actually in use,
 * even though the underlying blocks/brewguide-article-tasting-info.liquid and
 * sections/brewguide-article-info.liquid were correctly synced and the article's
 * own accentuate.* data was confirmed correct.
 *
 * Only the Brew Guides blog uses template_suffix "article" -- confirmed by
 * checking every other blog's articles (News: all use "news", resolving to the
 * separate, untouched templates/article.news.json; Flagship stores: all use the
 * default; Recipes and News (legacy "news-1") have no articles). The hundreds of
 * retired/orphaned Brew Guides articles not linked to any current product use the
 * default suffix too, so they already render from templates/article.json. Keep
 * this file identical to templates/article.json -- both are needed because
 * Shopify does not fall back from a named suffix to the default template when
 * the suffixed file is present but a *different* one is missing elsewhere; they
 * are two independent entry points into the same main-blog-post section, and the
 * brewguide-article-* blocks/sections are themselves gated on blog.handle == 'brewguides'
 * (PR #287: article.blog.handle resolves blank in this theme's actual rendering, despite
 * being documented Liquid -- use the global `blog` object instead), so this stays inert on
 * any article this template might ever end up serving outside that blog.
 */
